<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Japan Bonus Take-Home Calculator — Withholding Rate Table (2026) | yuzucalc"
  description="Net pay from a Japanese bonus: premiums on the standard bonus base, withholding from the official bonus rate table (2026, all 21 rates), validated against the NTA's worked example."
  path="/en/bonus/"
  altPath="/bonus/"
>
  <h1>Japan bonus take-home calculator</h1>
  <p class="lede">Bonus withholding in Japan does not use the monthly table. The rate comes from a separate table keyed by <strong>last month's pay after social insurance</strong> and your dependent count.</p>
  <p><span class="stamp">Bonus rate table: 2026 (all 21 rates) <span class="ok">Validated on {validation.passed}/{validation.total} official examples</span></span></p>

  <BonusCalc lang="en" />

  <h2>How bonus withholding works</h2>
  <div class="formula">Bonus income tax = (bonus − bonus premiums) × rate (from last month's taxable pay + dependents)</div>
  <p>Rates run from 0% to 45.945% in 21 steps. At the same prior-month pay of ¥196,616, the rate is 4.084% with no dependents and 2.042% with two. This calculator carries the full table and is validated on the NTA's own example (bonus ¥554,000, prior-month ¥196,616, 2 dependents → tax ¥9,585).</p>
  <h3>No prior-month salary?</h3>
  <p>New hires and similar cases switch to the <strong>monthly-table method</strong>: (bonus − premiums) ÷ 6 (÷ 12 if the bonus basis period exceeds 6 months), looked up in the monthly table, then multiplied back. The calculator switches automatically. The same fallback applies when the bonus exceeds 10× the prior month's pay.</p>
  <h3>Bonus premiums</h3>
  <p>Premiums are charged on the standard bonus amount (bonus truncated to ¥1,000): health/care/child levy capped at a cumulative ¥5.73M per year, pension capped at ¥1.5M per payment, employment insurance 0.5% (general) on the full amount. Resident tax is never deducted from a bonus — it is collected from monthly pay.</p>

  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <details class="acc"><summary>Is the bonus tax "too much"?</summary><div class="acc-body"><div class="acc-in"><div>The rate assumes the bonus repeats monthly, so it often over-withholds. It is settled in the year-end adjustment against your actual annual tax.</div></div></div></details>
    <details class="acc"><summary>Does overtime last month change my bonus tax?</summary><div class="acc-body"><div class="acc-in"><div>Yes — the rate depends only on last month's taxable pay. A heavy overtime month can push the bonus into a higher rate band (settled at year-end).</div></div></div></details>
  </div>

